  "name": "Ad Superpowers",
  "url": "https://mcp.adsuperpowers.ai/v1",
  "description": "Ad Superpowers is the control plane for supervised AI ad operations. It connects\nClaude to the advertising accounts a team already runs, so a question that normally\nmeans opening eight dashboards can be asked once.\n\nSupervision is the design, not a setting. Reads are the default: of 51 tools, 33 are\nread-only and 17 can write. Every tool declares readOnlyHint, destructiveHint and\nopenWorldHint, so the client can prompt before anything changes state. New ads are\ncreated paused. Writes are scoped to the connected account, throttled per account to protect account standing, and capped by per-plan quotas. Actions land in an audit log the organisation can read and export. Client profiles are versioned and restorable,\nand nothing is deleted through MCP.\n\nIt covers Meta, Google Ads, Google Analytics 4, Google Search Console, Google Tag\nManager, Google Merchant Center, LinkedIn and TikTok. Alongside the tools it ships\n120 skills and 29 workflows carrying the benchmarks and decision frameworks that make an answer useful rather than merely accurate: what counts as creative fatigue on TikTok versus Meta, which conversion number to trust when two platforms disagree, what a healthy cost per lead looks like on LinkedIn. Teams can write their own skills and workflows and save them to the organisation, so house method becomes something the assistant applies instead of something people have to remember.\n\nAgencies get client profiles as first-class context: budgets, channel goals, linked\nad accounts and standing attention points per client, so an answer is framed by the\naccount it concerns.\n\nThis is ad management, not ad serving. It reports on and adjusts campaigns the user\nalready owns, with credentials granted per platform and revocable at any time. It\ndoes not buy media, place inventory or deliver advertising. Built in Europe, for\nteams managing multiple clients, channels and people.",
